            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MOOLATTE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a fantastic recipe! It was easy, tasty, and colorful. I only made a few changes, regarding sweetness. I reduced the soy sauce to two teaspoons, because I felt it to be too overpowering. Also, I added about a teaspoon or so of white sugar (again, because of the soy sauce), and a few spoons of extra mayo. For color... I was definitely not shy with the dill, I added quite a bit extra."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Colette Castro"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Way too hot to cook! Made spinach salad and was looking for a honey mustard dressing. The ingredients looked a little strange... mayo and soy sauce and dill. But it was fabulous! I used stone ground and garlic aioli mustards, Tamari for soy sauce. I mixed it in a shakable jar and it was so thick I could not pour it out so I added a TBSP or so of olive oil to thin it out. Really delicious. Smack!",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-10T03:00:53.090Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
